WEBVTT

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:03.200
We meet again.

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:07.590
Welcome to last episode's dazzling recap!

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:12.740
In order to enter the 
Junior Youth Championship,

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:16.000
Yuya challenged the quiz king Eita Kyuando!

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:18.280
Depending on whether you give 
the right or wrong answers,

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.420
Action Card effects change on this field.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.400
Unable to answer a single question 
correctly, Yuya is feeling the pressure!

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:31.580
And there's another man 
who's feeling the pressure!

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:42.970
I'm still missing something!

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:50.230
Implementing mass into Solid 
Vision has created Action Duels.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:55.080
In duels where the field, monsters 
and duelists become one,

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:58.600
the people are caught in 
a frenzy of excitement!

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:02.410
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:21.190
You!  The strongest card 
isn't about winning or losing

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.600
You!  At full speed  On the game

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.340
Swinging ma ma ma mind

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:37.910
The soul's pendulum  Ultimate confusion

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.110
Impulse  Got it got it

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:45.320
Tough battles  Real revolution

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:56.080
Everybody goin'  Break through the walls!

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:03.000
Infinite future  Get rid of indecision!

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.940
Make it Make it  Be courageous (Break it now)

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:10.340
Step ahead!  Take a step (Do it now)

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:20.620
The fun is only getting started!  
So everyone's a Believer!!

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.960
Believe x Believe  Biri-Biri-Biri Buddies!

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:34.000
Difficult Questions!?  Attack Duel Quiz!!

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.910
I activate an Action Card!

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:43.250
The heaven of knowledge will 
guide the stupid to hell!

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:47.250
Quiz Quest - Extra Stage!

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.250
What is this field?

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:05.250
Yuya Sakaki, you'll fully 
realize your own stupidity.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.820
He's been dueling perfectly so far.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:15.070
That is why he's Clarity School's ace!

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:20.800
We're going to pass through 
five Action Traps.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.380
Action Traps?

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:24.910
So more quizzes?

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.280
Yes!

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:29.540
If you're correct, you gain 100 life points.

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:32.690
If you're incorrect, you 
take 100 points of damage.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:36.400
Have a wonderful quiz journey!  Adieu!

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.620
Quiz journey?

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:45.020
What's that?

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:46.710
Action Card?

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:48.740
It's huge!

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.540
Action Trap activates.

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:55.810
Attack Duel Quiz!

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:57.480
Duel Quiz?

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.880
It's a question about dueling?

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.940
I can handle that!

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:04.680
Yuya is an expert at dueling!

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:05.480
Yeah!

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:06.970
Question!

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:11.200
Here are two Raigeki Break 
cards.  Which one is correct?

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.310
The time limit is 5 seconds!

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:16.770
The correct one?  Umm...

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:17.900
Which is it?

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.370
Which is it?

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.770
Too bad!  Time's up!

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:25.840
The correct answer is the right one!

00:04:25.840 --> 00:04:28.170
Oh yeah!

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:31.710
Since you couldn't answer, you 
take 100 points of damage.

00:04:33.550 --> 00:04:36.570
He's shivering!

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:37.540
Question!

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.910
How many teeth does Pot of Greed have?

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:42.690
Twenty!

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:44.970
Correct!

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:48.170
Pot of Greed has twenty teeth.

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:50.270
You gain 100 life points.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:55.120
I'm in trouble if things don't change.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:57.770
All right!  From my hand...

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.800
Wait a second!

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.050
Question!

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:06.620
How many people are flying in Heavy Storm?

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:08.620
The time limit is 5 seconds!

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.020
That's easy!

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:12.910
Two people!

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:14.340
Two!

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:15.880
Too bad.

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:17.710
The correct answer is three people.

00:05:18.340 --> 00:05:19.570
Three people?

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:21.520
Yes, three people.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.380
One.

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:23.880
Two.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:26.540
Three!

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.680
There was another person there?

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.710
Since you were incorrect, you 
take 100 points of damage.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.480
He's spinning!

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.480
He's silly!

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:45.480
So funny!

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:49.030
Your goal isn't to make them laugh!

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.800
The correct answer is...

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:31.310
Only one!

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:40.800
This is bad.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:44.050
His answers were all wrong, so 
he's down to 300 life points.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:49.480
Kyuando answered every question 
correctly, so he has 6300 life points!

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:57.860
You must now realize that challenging me 
on this field is completely incorrect!

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:00.400
I am going to win this duel!

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:03.540
That is the perfectly correct answer!

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:05.710
Correct answer!

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:10.540
Ah-choo!

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:13.510
You're so lame.

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:19.140
Ah-choo!  Ah-choo!

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:22.740
It seems...

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:24.460
...they're entertained.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.430
Thank you.

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:34.510
Hey!

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:41.940
Instead of watching me shine, you're 
entertained by this dumb loser?  That's stupid!

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:45.310
The real performance is about to begin!

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:49.820
I activate the spell card Performapal 
Recasting from my hand!

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:54.570
I return five Performapals 
in my hand to the deck.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:08:00.960
Then I draw the same number of cards I 
returned plus one, so I draw six cards!

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:04.160
Yeah!  I got them!

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:12.110
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 1 
Stargazer Magician and Scale 8 Timegazer Magician!

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:29.050
Now I can summon monsters between 
Level 2 and 7 simultaneously!

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:32.040
Swing, my soul's pendulum!

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:34.990
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:37.000
Pendulum Summon!

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.540
Come out, my monsters!

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:44.700
Performapal Lizardraw!

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:47.210
Performapal Whip Snake!

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:51.540
And Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:55.680
This is Pendulum Summon!

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.510
No biggie.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:03.960
Now he can destroy Kyuando's monsters!

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:09.460
But Kyuando has his Quiz 
Monkey-Not So Fast! combo.

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:12.660
Too bad!  The correct answer is one monster!

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:16.640
Since you answered zero, you're incorrect!

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:18.130
Too bad!

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:21.060
I won't use Not So Fast! this time!

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.400
Therefore, the correct answer is zero!

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:25.610
You're incorrect!

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:30.550
No matter what Yuya answers, the 
combo makes sure he's wrong.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:32.600
No, it'll be fine!

00:09:33.250 --> 00:09:37.330
Not So Fast!'s effect can 
only be used once per turn.

00:09:37.330 --> 00:09:40.560
Yuya currently has three monsters.

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:43.260
Even if he's negated once,

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:46.460
three monsters are enough to 
eliminate Kyuando's monsters.

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:47.900
I see!

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:49.930
Here I go!  Let's battle!

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:53.060
Whip Snake, attack Quiz Monkey!

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:55.530
Quiz Monkey's effect activates!

00:09:55.530 --> 00:10:02.530
When it battles, you have to answer 
a question before the battle begins.

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:03.660
Here it comes!

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:04.840
Question!

00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:10.590
How many Quiz Monsters will be on 
the field at the end of this battle?

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:12.660
I'll get it right this time!

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:14.780
The answer is zero!

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.460
Go, Whip Snake!

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:18.600
Destroy Quiz Monkey!

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:21.800
Too bad, but that won't happen.

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.270
Quiz Sphinx's effect activates!

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:33.330
Once per turn, you have to answer a 
question when you attack a Quiz Monster.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:37.600
Quiz Sphinx also asks questions?

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:41.720
It's a simple and easy question.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:48.400
Which monster currently on the 
field has the highest Level?

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:52.660
If you answer correctly, 
that monster is destroyed,

00:10:52.990 --> 00:10:57.000
and its controller takes damage 
equal to its attack points.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:02.110
If you're incorrect, the battle ends!

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:03.660
That's easy.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:08.530
The monster with the highest 
Level is Level 7 Odd-Eyes.

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:10.650
You're such a fool.

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:11.730
Why?

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:13.460
Didn't you hear its effect?

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:16.010
If Yuya answers correctly and says Odd-Eyes.

00:11:16.010 --> 00:11:20.930
Odd-Eyes will be destroyed, and 
he'll take 2500 points of damage.

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:24.330
If that happens, Yuya loses.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:30.670
In order to avoid losing, I 
have to give the wrong answer.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:32.800
Exactly!

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:38.200
But give the correct answer if you want.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:43.600
Give your answer.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:54.430
Which monster currently on the 
field has the highest Level?

00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:56.600
Give your answer.

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:01.670
Quiz Monkey.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:08.330
Yeah, you had to answer incorrectly!

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:15.260
Too bad!  Since your answer 
is incorrect, the battle ends!

00:12:15.260 --> 00:12:20.730
Your answer to Quiz Monkey's 
question was zero.

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:22.200
Oh my!

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:27.660
The battle ended, but there 
are two monsters on my field.

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:32.200
That means you answered this 
question incorrectly too!

00:12:33.070 --> 00:12:36.930
So one of your monsters is destroyed.

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:41.860
I will destroy Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:12:45.260 --> 00:12:50.200
In the end, Odd-Eyes was destroyed.

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:57.400
Due to its destruction, Quiz Monkey's attack 
points become the same as Odd-Eyes's.

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:01.860
Pendulum Monsters don't go the graveyard.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:04.000
They go to the Extra Deck.

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:10.770
You escaped defeat, but what can 
you do from this point forward?

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:15.070
I activate Lizardraw's effect.

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:19.540
Once per turn, when my monster is destroyed,

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:24.000
I draw one card for every 
Performapal on the field.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:26.290
There are two Performapals on my field!

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:30.790
Therefore, I draw two cards!

00:13:31.600 --> 00:13:34.660
Good!  I still have a way to win!

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:39.200
I set three cards and end my turn!

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:47.800
You have zero cards in your hand.

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:50.810
That means you'll rely on Action Cards.

00:13:50.810 --> 00:13:53.050
My turn!  Let's battle!

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:57.330
Quiz Monkey, attack Whip Snake!

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:00.820
I activate the trap Last Minute Cancel!

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:06.730
This card switches all my 
monsters to defense position.

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:12.600
And any Performapals destroyed in 
battle this turn return to my hand!

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:24.260
I return Performapal Whip Snake to my hand!

00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:26.000
Here's the next battle!

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:29.860
Quiz Sphinx, attack Performapal Lizardraw!

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:36.060
I return Performapal Lizardraw to my hand!

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:40.530
I activate the Quick-Play Spell 
Double It!! from my hand!

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:45.930
When a Level 4-or-above Quiz Monster 
destroys a monster in defense position...

00:14:46.180 --> 00:14:51.400
...its attack points double until the end 
of the turn, and it can attack again!

00:14:51.400 --> 00:14:54.370
Unless things change, he'll 
take a direct attack!

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:58.530
Quiz Sphinx attacks Yuya Sakaki directly!

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:00.530
This is the end!

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:02.130
No, not yet!

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:07.000
I don't think that Action Card will suit you.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:08.690
That's fine!

00:15:08.690 --> 00:15:14.130
He must be desperate because that 
question is worth 5000 life points.

00:15:14.660 --> 00:15:16.130
Here goes!

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:20.900
I activate an Action Trap!

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:24.440
Quiz action!

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:28.300
You chose the genre Math for 5000.

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:30.910
Math?  That's a bad choice!

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:32.130
Question!

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:36.180
Prove Fermat's Last Theorem.

00:15:38.800 --> 00:15:40.550
That's an easy question!

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:42.350
At least for me!

00:15:42.350 --> 00:15:44.360
The time limit is 5 seconds.

00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:50.130
I have no idea.

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:53.300
You're not going to answer?

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:56.000
I didn't have to do a thing.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:16:00.250
Since you're wrong, you take 5000 
points of damage and lose.  Adieu!

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:01.900
It's fine that I'm wrong.

00:16:02.570 --> 00:16:06.810
I activate the trap Performapal Reborn Force!

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:09.050
When a Performapal is destroyed,

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:13.990
the effect damage that I take that 
turn is dealt to you instead once!

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:15.400
What?

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.260
Go!

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:29.940
If this effect activates during 
battle, the battle ends.

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:31.250
He did it!

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:33.550
I'm getting shivers!

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.370
Unbelievable!

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:39.850
Kyuando took damage!

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:44.650
You used an incorrect answer to 
your advantage?  Unbelievable!

00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:50.350
Answering a question correctly doesn't 
mean it's the correct thing to do.

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:52.950
Because this is a quiz duel.

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:55.030
A duel.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:17:02.430
I am fully aware of that!

00:17:02.600 --> 00:17:06.850
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:13.380
Double It!!'s effect ends, so Quiz 
Sphinx's attack points return to normal.

00:17:13.570 --> 00:17:15.010
My turn!

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:17.850
The fun is only getting started!

00:17:19.850 --> 00:17:23.020
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:26.520
Since the Pendulum Scale has been set,

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:31.760
I can summon monsters between 
Level 2 and 7 simultaneously.

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:35.850
Let's begin!

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:38.400
Swing, my soul's pendulum!

00:17:38.650 --> 00:17:41.370
Draw an arc of light in the sky!

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:43.350
Pendulum Summon!

00:17:46.600 --> 00:17:49.700
First is Performapal Hip Hippo!

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:55.700
Next, the Performapal monsters 
that left earlier now return!

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:57.960
Performapal Whip Snake!

00:17:58.350 --> 00:18:00.500
Performapal Lizardraw!

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:06.370
And the radiant one with different-colored 
eyes!  Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:12.610
I activate the trap Final Question!

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:13.900
Question!

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:18.440
How many monsters are on the field 
at the start of this battle?

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:21.080
Another quiz!

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:24.150
If you're correct, all my 
monsters are destroyed.

00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:27.750
If you're incorrect, all 
your monsters are destroyed.

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:30.400
Now answer.

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:33.950
There are two on your field and four on mine.

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:36.900
The answer is six!  Let's battle!

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:38.500
You fell for it!

00:18:38.500 --> 00:18:40.150
I activate a trap!

00:18:40.150 --> 00:18:41.450
Card Chute!

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:44.780
Quiz Sphinx gains attack points equal

00:18:44.780 --> 00:18:48.150
to a Level 4-or-below Quiz 
Monster's attack points.

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:52.650
In other words, it gains 
Quiz Monkey's 2500 points.

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:56.450
Then Quiz Monkey returns to my hand!

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:02.000
That means there are five monsters on 
the field at the start of this battle!

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:05.950
Your answer of six is incorrect!

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:10.160
All your monsters are destroyed!

00:19:13.350 --> 00:19:15.360
I have an overwhelming advantage!

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:17.900
This is correct!  Very correct!

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:20.970
It's time for a question!

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:24.940
Who will be the winner of this duel?

00:19:26.250 --> 00:19:29.050
Me, of course.

00:19:29.050 --> 00:19:30.560
We'll see about that.

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:35.000
Watch closely!

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:40.290
When the smoke clears, 
there will be a surprise!

00:19:40.290 --> 00:19:44.200
When you see it, give a round of applause!

00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:50.000
No way!

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:54.200
Why?  Why?  Why?  Why?

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:58.550
The trap card Performapal Curtain Call!

00:19:59.000 --> 00:20:02.100
Its effect negated Odd-Eyes's destruction.

00:20:02.450 --> 00:20:05.480
And until the end of this turn,

00:20:05.480 --> 00:20:10.500
Odd-Eyes gains 600 attack points for 
every Performapal that was destroyed.

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:12.750
Here I go!

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:16.750
Odd-Eyes Pendulum Dragon attacks Quiz Sphinx!

00:20:16.750 --> 00:20:18.200
You fool!

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:20.900
Did you forget about Quiz Sphinx's effect?

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:25.650
If you attack a Quiz Monster, 
you have to answer a question.

00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:28.560
The monster affected by Curtain Call

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:32.480
can negate your spells, 
traps and monster effects!

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:34.100
What?

00:20:34.100 --> 00:20:37.300
Including the trap card Not So Fast!?

00:20:37.950 --> 00:20:40.190
Odd-Eyes's effect activates!

00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:48.000
When this card battles a Level 5-or-above 
monster, battle damage is doubled!

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:51.850
Therefore, you take 1600 points of damage!

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:56.350
No way!

00:20:56.350 --> 00:21:00.250
The winner of this duel is Yuya Sakaki!

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:03.600
Eita Kyuando, you were incorrect!

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:09.000
I was incorrect?

00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:11.050
I won.

00:21:11.050 --> 00:21:13.250
Congratulations, Yuya!

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:18.250
You never forgot your part in the duel 
and took on the field and cards head-on.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:23.200
A duel is how competitors 
communicate by using cards.

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:29.400
You made us remember how 
true dueling ought to be.

00:21:31.050 --> 00:21:34.800
Communication using cards...

00:21:41.280 --> 00:21:44.950
It gave me shivers!

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:51.700
Is that checkmate?

00:21:56.450 --> 00:22:01.800
President, we detected unimaginable Fusion 
Summon energies within Maiami City.

00:22:02.150 --> 00:22:03.600
I see.

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:07.350
So he's also winning.

00:22:13.460 --> 00:22:18.940
Catch the dream dancing in my heart
Release my falling tears

00:22:19.160 --> 00:22:28.420
I'll step out on to my first field
To meet my miracle  Fabulous One Step

00:22:35.310 --> 00:22:40.430
I realized that strength can't be given

00:22:40.690 --> 00:22:45.670
It's something I have to grab myself

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:51.110
In that case, I have to keep moving
I can't stay still

00:22:51.360 --> 00:22:56.370
Even if walls and headwinds block my way

00:22:56.570 --> 00:23:01.970
I'll draw my trump card called 
"courage" to take a step forward

00:23:01.970 --> 00:23:06.390
I believe in my story of victory

00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:12.360
Everyone during battle is My Way
Duelists are being tested

00:23:12.360 --> 00:23:17.770
When times are tough, that's when you 
Smile, Jump, Fight & Step Up!

00:23:17.770 --> 00:23:23.100
Your smile is your Energy
Kick away your feelings of running away

00:23:23.100 --> 00:23:32.440
Jump into the new field
Shiny One Step that leads to the future

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:40.660
One step... Just one step is fine
That's your Big Chance!!

00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:51.020
Yuzu is trying to improve by 
learning Fusion Summon from Sora,

00:23:51.020 --> 00:23:53.380
but what should I do?

00:23:53.380 --> 00:23:55.950
Ouch!  Don't suddenly get in my way!

00:23:55.950 --> 00:23:58.450
You're the one who bumped into me!

00:23:58.450 --> 00:24:00.260
Hokuto, we have to go!

00:24:00.260 --> 00:24:01.420
Right.

00:24:01.420 --> 00:24:02.750
Did something happen?

00:24:02.750 --> 00:24:06.200
We found the attacker!  The mystery duelist!

00:24:06.200 --> 00:24:06.860
What?

00:24:07.230 --> 00:24:11.430
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V:
Beyond Pendulum

00:24:11.430 --> 00:24:13.550
The fun is only getting started!
